General chemistry (@general-chemistry: 0, is #chapter, #general-chemistry "Reading-from-zero.lingua#r_0470T6ZDV7KCP63TE2D5GX9ANG") { r_206GS6CVXD8WSY1VX7PRF7136V
Understand substances, structure, transformations, and chemical evidence from an accessible beginning through advanced practical and scholarly investigation. The same quantitative, measurement, and computational foundations connect minerals, water, materials, biology, manufacture, and technology without dissolving their unique knowledge into a short overview.

**Start:** [Begin general chemistry from zero](Reading-from-zero.lingua#r_0470T6ZDV7KCP63TE2D5GX9ANG). No previous chemistry course is assumed. Work through substantial whole books and problems, use original explanations and independently checkable examples, and follow missing preparation when it is actually needed. Later laboratory, coupled-equilibrium, kinetic, material-chain, and independent research work provides the demanding depth.

| Part | Connected readings |
| --- | --- |
| Opening questions, language, and quantities | [Begin general chemistry from zero](Reading-from-zero.lingua#r_0470T6ZDV7KCP63TE2D5GX9ANG) · [Ask a chemical question about a material and a change](foundations/A-chemical-question.lingua#r_7Y7E3QBYQADPGQ06JXY84FCEVN) · [Substances, mixtures, components, and phases](foundations/Substances-mixtures-and-phases.lingua#r_07Y9PYVRA9HSVSZWQC4N0X8ZZS) · [Connect observations, particle models, and chemical symbols](foundations/Observations-particles-and-symbols.lingua#r_1BMJ0JMYA9THS9B5K12C423YFC) · [Read formulas and names without losing chemical identity](foundations/Formulas-names-and-charge.lingua#r_1CP96XH8H24BQWR2PEA3CT4H61) · [Atomic models are explanations constrained by evidence](atomic/Evidence-for-atoms-and-nuclei.lingua#r_4HT48V97KV1TDBR18MBRR0HCE4) · [Isotopic composition, atomic mass, and a material’s molar mass](atomic/Isotopes-and-atomic-weights.lingua#r_7RS9YA931BVZ7RVM0KSWJ2W7Y3) · [Units, dimensions, and equations that can make sense](../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/foundations/Units-and-dimensions.lingua#r_3A511KGNX59K2YHKT83NM38NE1) · [Convert mass, amount of substance, and numbers of specified entities](quantities/Mass-amount-and-entities.lingua#r_5FWGQX84V6GZGC1RABD34ZKE04) · [Let measurement information determine the precision of a chemical claim](quantities/Precision-uncertainty-and-chemical-claims.lingua#r_25GXFBHM1573BAYA8PFWH0YW97) |
